Omarchy: EDA_BASE_FRAME::RecreateToolbars() dereferenced a null m_toolbarSettings
for frames that have none (the KiPython scripting console).  Changing any
preference broadcasts CommonSettingsChanged() to every open frame, so KiCad 10.0.6
segfaulted in TOOLBAR_SETTINGS::GetToolbarConfig on the first Preferences OK with
the console present.  Unchanged in 10.0.8; not reported upstream as of 2026-11-18.

--- a/common/eda_base_frame.cpp
+++ b/common/eda_base_frame.cpp
@@ -771,6 +771,13 @@
 
     wxASSERT( m_toolbarSettings );
 
+    // A frame without toolbar settings -- the KiPython scripting console -- has
+    // no toolbars to rebuild.  CommonSettingsChanged() calls this on every open
+    // frame, and the wxASSERT above is compiled out of release builds, so
+    // changing any preference while the console existed dereferenced null.
+    if( !m_toolbarSettings )
+        return;
+
     if( m_tbRight )
         m_tbRight->ClearToolbar();
 
